; A count follow read as no choice (S-0138-e, the bidder's first reading; the
; same reading as C8, p. 54, S-0078-c). Hand 31 (deuces, 30), the bidder after
; trick one: he led the 2-2, and the right setter followed with the 3-2, a
; trump that is count. Read under protect-the-count (a setter following a
; bidder's lead that cannot lose keeps his count when he has a follower
; without it), the right setter held no other trump, so every trump the bidder
; does not hold is the left setter's. Asked from the bidder's seat:
;
;   silas query examples/book/reading/left-setter-holds-the-trumps-out.silas \
;     --hand hand-31 --trick 2 --seat bidder \
;     --read right=examples/book/protect-the-count.silas
;
; Uniform: 5/22. Read: 1, exact given protect-the-count as the right setter's
; policy (tests/book_reading.rs).
(include book)

(query
  (left-setter s)
  (trump q)
  (none (roles t) (in t q) (live t) (not (mine t)) (not (holds s t))))
